          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದೈತ್ಯ — daitya — \"a giant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಥೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಒಬ್ಬ ದೈತ್ಯ ಬೆಟ್ಟದ ಮೇಲೆ ಇದ್ದನು. katheyalli obba daitya beṭṭada mēle iddanu. In the story a giant lived on the hill."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ದೈತ್ಯರು, daityaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "As an adjective it means huge: ದೈತ್ಯ (daitya) ಮರ, a giant tree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದೈತ್ಯ (daitya) is borrowed from Sanskrit daitya, the name of a race of demons in the old stories (Monier-Williams); in Kannada it also means a giant."
            }
          ]
